    <h1 class="headline">The Aravalli hearing is open to the public</h1>

    <div class="utility-row">
      <span class="source-line">Source: <b>Supreme Court High-Powered Committee</b> · Suo Motu Writ 10/2025</span>
      <button class="listen-btn" data-article="brd-aravalli"><span class="bars"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="lbl-text">Listen to this article</span></button>
    </div>

    <figure class="article-image">
      <img src="/assets/images/aravalli.jpg" alt="Public campaigners calling for protection of the Aravallis" width="690" height="388" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <figcaption>Campaigners calling for protection of the Aravalli range.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="visual-block">
      <div class="visual-label">How To Make A Representation</div>
      <div class="visual-frame">
        <div class="deadline"><span class="dl">Committee must report by</span><span class="dv">31 August 2026</span></div>
        <div class="facts" style="margin-bottom:16px"><div class="fl">Who the committee wants to hear from</div><table>
          <tr><td class="k">Communities</td><td>Villagers, farmers, mine-workers and local communities whose livelihoods are tied to the range.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="k">Organisations</td><td>Environmentalists and non-profit organisations working on the Aravallis.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="k">Industry</td><td>Mining lease-holders and project proponents.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="k">How to send</td><td>Via the committee's form, or by email to <b>mshpcaravalli@gmail.com</b>. Submissions carry more weight when backed by documents or verifiable material.</td></tr>
        </table></div>
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="rchip">Delhi</span><span class="rchip">Rajasthan</span><span class="rchip">Haryana</span><span class="rchip">Gujarat</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="visual-caption">The four states the committee has invited representations from.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="supporting-copy">
      <p>The Supreme Court has set up a High-Powered Committee on the Aravalli Hills and Ranges, and it has to report by <b>31 August 2026</b>. Until then it is taking representations from anyone affected by mining, land use or conservation in the range.</p>
      <p>This is a direct channel into a Supreme Court-mandated process — the sort of thing normally reached through lawyers, industry associations and well-funded intervenors. The people whose livelihoods sit closest to the range are the ones least likely to know the window exists. And the window is short: <span class="stat st-red">21 days</span> from the notice.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <span class="co-k">If you know someone affected, forward this</span>
      <p>Submissions go via the committee's form, or by email to <b>mshpcaravalli@gmail.com</b>. Confirm the exact closing date before relying on it — the notice period runs from publication, not from the reporting deadline.</p>
    </div>
