    <h1 class="headline">'Gems of India' — a paid national stage for grassroots creators</h1>

    <div class="utility-row">
      <span class="source-line">Source: <b>Ministry of Information &amp; Broadcasting</b> (PIB)</span>
      <button class="listen-btn" data-article="brd-gems"><span class="bars"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="lbl-text">Listen to this article</span></button>
    </div>

    <figure class="article-image">
      <img src="/assets/images/gems-of-india.webp" alt="A grassroots film crew working on location in an Indian village" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <figcaption>A small film crew working on location—the kind of district-level storytelling the programme seeks.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="visual-block">
      <div class="visual-label">The Awards Ladder</div>
      <div class="visual-frame">
        <div class="ladder">
          <div class="rung"><div class="rl">District</div><div class="rv">₹50,000</div><div class="rd">Up to 20 awards at this level, per district</div></div>
          <div class="rung"><div class="rl">State</div><div class="rv">₹2 lakh</div><div class="rd">For one standout creator from each district</div></div>
          <div class="rung"><div class="rl">National</div><div class="rv">₹5 lakh</div><div class="rd">Each, for selected entries in the national rollout</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="deadline" style="margin:16px 0 0"><span class="dl">Entries open</span><span class="dv">1–31 August 2026</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="visual-caption">A 1–3 minute video, uploaded to the MyWAVES section of the WAVES OTT platform.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="supporting-copy">
      <p>The Information &amp; Broadcasting Ministry wants creators to film their own district — its culture, heritage, tourism and history — as a <b>1–3 minute video</b>, uploaded to the MyWAVES section of the WAVES OTT platform. Entries run <span class="stat st-blue">1–31 August 2026</span>. Prasar Bharati, My Bharat, YouTube and Meta are partners.</p>
      <p>The awards are money, not exposure: up to twenty district awards of ₹50,000, ₹2 lakh for a standout creator from each district, and ₹5 lakh each at the national level.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="visual-block" style="margin-top:26px">
      <div class="visual-label">Pilot Regions</div>
      <div class="visual-frame">
        <div class="chip-row">
          <span class="rchip">Andaman &amp; Nicobar</span><span class="rchip">Arunachal Pradesh</span><span class="rchip">Chandigarh</span>
          <span class="rchip">Dadra &amp; Nagar Haveli and Daman &amp; Diu</span><span class="rchip">Goa</span><span class="rchip">Ladakh</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="visual-caption">A nationwide rollout is to follow the pilot.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="supporting-copy">
      <p>Look at the pilot list again. Andaman &amp; Nicobar. Arunachal Pradesh. Ladakh. Dadra &amp; Nagar Haveli. These are the places that appear least often in national programming — and, as this edition's own data shows, among the least likely to come up in Parliament either.</p>
      <p>If you are a creator in one of these regions, or you can pass this on to youth groups, colleges and cultural organisations there, it is an unusually direct route to money and to a national platform, with no gatekeeper in the middle.</p>
    </div>
